From a8114ad8da01c89f64e3983f6ebad37184f1ffbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdndds <rdndds@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:05:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] BpfNetMaps: do not abort init when stats config update fails

On some 4.14 kernels (e.g. Infinix X6812B 4.14.186), BPF_MAP_UPDATE_ELEM
on BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY succeeds for key 0 but returns EINVAL for any
non-zero key.

In initBpfMaps(), sConfigurationMap opens and updates key 0
(UID_RULES_CONFIGURATION_KEY), then fails with EINVAL on key 1
(CURRENT_STATS_MAP_CONFIGURATION_KEY) and aborts before opening
sUidOwnerMap and the remaining maps. When the init exception is caught,
sConfigurationMap remains non-null while sUidOwnerMap is null:
ConnectivityService/NPMS subsequently enable BACKGROUND_MATCH and
OEM_DENY_1_MATCH in map_netd_configuration_map[0], while setUidRule()
no-ops, leaving map_netd_uid_owner_map empty and blocking networking
and DNS for all non-system UIDs in netd and kernel cgroupskb/cgroupsock.

Log a warning instead of aborting on CURRENT_STATS_MAP_CONFIGURATION_KEY
(index 1 is already zero-initialized to SELECT_MAP_A by the kernel), and
clear sConfigurationMap if init still aborts before sUidOwnerMap opens.

Change-Id: Ib246440d559b5a3d994b82ab223833e42aff6e1f
---
 service/src/com/android/server/BpfNetMaps.java | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/service/src/com/android/server/BpfNetMaps.java b/service/src/com/android/server/BpfNetMaps.java
index 8f57ad7..ee57329 100644
--- a/service/src/com/android/server/BpfNetMaps.java
+++ b/service/src/com/android/server/BpfNetMaps.java
@@ -262,7 +262,7 @@ public class BpfNetMaps {
             sConfigurationMap.updateEntry(CURRENT_STATS_MAP_CONFIGURATION_KEY,
                     new U32(STATS_SELECT_MAP_A));
         } catch (ErrnoException e) {
-            throw new IllegalStateException("Failed to initialize current stats configuration", e);
+            Log.w(TAG, "Failed to initialize current stats configuration, continuing", e);
         }
 
         if (sUidOwnerMap == null) {
@@ -372,6 +372,9 @@ public class BpfNetMaps {
             try {
                 ensureInitialized(context);
             } catch (Throwable t) {
+                if (sUidOwnerMap == null) {
+                    sConfigurationMap = null;
+                }
                 Log.e(TAG, "Failed to initialize BPF maps", t);
             }
         }
-- 
